   $q$Starting at point $A_1$ on a circle, Priya keeps the compass at the radius and marks six points $A_1, A_2, A_3, A_4, A_5, A_6$ in order around the circle. Which three points should Priya connect to form an equilateral triangle inscribed in the circle?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$A_1$, $A_3$ and $A_5$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$A_1$, $A_2$ and $A_3$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"connected-consecutive-points"},{"text":"$A_1$, $A_2$ and $A_4$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-uneven-spacing"},{"text":"$A_1$, $A_4$ and the center","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-diameter-and-center"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$A_1$, $A_3$ and $A_5$$q$, $q$Connecting every other point splits the circle into three equal arcs of $120^\circ$, giving an equilateral triangle. Consecutive points $A_1$, $A_2$, $A_3$ give a triangle with two short sides and one long side.$q$, 'draft', null)
