   $q$Ray $YK$ bisects $\angle XYZ$, which measures $118^\circ$. Ray $YL$ is then constructed to bisect $\angle XYK$. What is the measure of $\angle LYZ$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$88.5^\\circ$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$59^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"stopped-after-one-bisection"},{"text":"$29.5^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"found-xyl-instead"},{"text":"$147.5^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-to-whole-angle"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$88.5^\circ$$q$, $q$$\angle KYZ = 118^\circ \div 2 = 59^\circ$ and $\angle LYK = 59^\circ \div 2 = 29.5^\circ$, so $\angle LYZ = 29.5^\circ + 59^\circ = 88.5^\circ$. The choice $29.5^\circ$ is $\angle XYL$, the small piece next to ray $YX$.$q$, 'draft', null)
