   $q$A town wants a new water well at a point equally far from three farmhouses at points $A$, $B$ and $C$, which do not lie on one line. Which construction locates the well?$q$, $q$[{"text":"construct the perpendicular from $A$ to $\\overline{BC}$ and use its midpoint","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-altitude"},{"text":"bisect $\\angle A$ and $\\angle B$ and use the point where the bisectors cross","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confused-with-incenter"},{"text":"join each farmhouse to the midpoint of the opposite side and use the point where these segments cross","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confused-with-centroid"},{"text":"construct the perpendicular bisectors of $\\overline{AB}$ and $\\overline{BC}$ and use the point where they cross","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$construct the perpendicular bisectors of $\overline{AB}$ and $\overline{BC}$ and use the point where they cross$q$, $q$Every point on the perpendicular bisector of $\overline{AB}$ is equally far from $A$ and $B$, and likewise for $\overline{BC}$, so their crossing point is equally far from all three. Angle bisectors meet at a point equally far from the sides of the triangle, not from its vertices.$q$, 'draft', null)
