  ('1744b2d7-0451-518b-b99d-b79b07d198f6', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'math-g10-constructions'), null, 'hard',
   $q$While copying $\angle ABC$, Felipe draws an arc of radius $6$ cm centered at $B$ that crosses the sides at $D$ and $F$. Felipe measures the chord $DF = 6\sqrt{2}$ cm. What is the measure of $\angle ABC$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$120^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-chord-for-120-degrees"},{"text":"$45^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"read-root-two-as-45-degrees"},{"text":"$60^\\circ$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"assumed-equilateral"},{"text":"$90^\\circ$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$90^\circ$$q$, $q$Triangle $DBF$ has $BD = BF = 6$ and $DF = 6\sqrt{2}$, and $6^2 + 6^2 = 72 = (6\sqrt{2})^2$, so the angle at $B$ is $90^\circ$. A $60^\circ$ angle would give a chord of $6$, equal to the radius.$q$, 'draft', null)
