   $q$A quilter constructs a square inscribed in a circle of radius $8$ inches by drawing two perpendicular diameters. What is the area of the square, in square inches?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$128$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$64$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-radius-as-side"},{"text":"$64\\pi$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"found-circle-area"},{"text":"$256$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-diameter-as-side"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$128$$q$, $q$The side is $8\sqrt{2}$, so the area is $(8\sqrt{2})^2 = 128$; equivalently, the diagonals are $16$ and the area is $\frac{16 \cdot 16}{2} = 128$. The choice $256$ treats the diameter as a side.$q$, 'draft', null)
