   $q$A regular hexagon is constructed in a circle of radius $6$. Joining each vertex to the center splits it into six triangles. What is the area of the hexagon?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$54$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dropped-the-radical"},{"text":"$54\\sqrt{3}$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$108\\sqrt{3}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-half-in-triangle-area"},{"text":"$9\\sqrt{3}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"found-one-triangle-only"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$54\sqrt{3}$$q$, $q$Each triangle is equilateral with side $6$, so its area is $\frac{\sqrt{3}}{4} \cdot 36 = 9\sqrt{3}$, and six of them give $54\sqrt{3}$. The choice $108\sqrt{3}$ uses base times height for each triangle without the factor $\frac{1}{2}$.$q$, 'draft', null)
