   $q$A stage designer marks points $A$ and $B$ that are $10$ m apart, then swings a $10$ m cord from each to find point $C$ where the arcs meet, forming an equilateral triangle. To the nearest tenth of a meter, how far is $C$ from line $AB$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$8.7$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$10.0$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-side-as-height"},{"text":"$5.0$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"used-half-side"},{"text":"$11.2$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-squares-instead-of-subtracting"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$8.7$$q$, $q$Point $C$ lies on the perpendicular bisector of $\overline{AB}$, so its distance to the line is $\sqrt{10^2 - 5^2} = \sqrt{75} = 5\sqrt{3} \approx 8.66$, which rounds to $8.7$ m. The choice $11.2$ comes from $\sqrt{10^2 + 5^2} \approx 11.18$, adding squares instead of subtracting.$q$, 'draft', null)
